a:54:{s:4:"body";a:3:{s:5:"value";s:1380:"<p>Log all <a href="https://api.drupal.org/api/drupal/core%21lib%21Drupal.php/function/Drupal%3A%3AhttpClient/8.9.x" target="_blank" rel="nofollow">drupal core http_client </a>request &amp; response logs in database. So it easily to track the outgoing traffic init by drupal http_client.</p>
<p><strong>Features:</strong><br />
1. This module logs all the request and response init by drupal core http client.<br />
2. provide web UI to manage the logs, for example: filter, view detail etc.</p>
<p><strong>How to use</strong>:<br />
1. composer require drupal/http_client_log<br />
2. drush en -y http_client_log<br />
3. using below code to verify request.</p>
<pre class="codeblock"><code class="language-php">use Drupal\Component\Serialization\Json;
$base_url = "https://httpbin.org";
$client = \Drupal::httpClient();

$response = $client-&gt;get($base_url . '/get');
$data = Json::Decode($response-&gt;getBody());
dpm($data);

$response = $client-&gt;get($base_url . '/anything', [
  'headers' =&gt; [
    'accept' =&gt; 'application/json'
  ],
]);
$data = Json::decode($response-&gt;getBody());
dpm($data);

$response = $client-&gt;post($base_url . '/status/500', [
  'verify' =&gt; true,
  'headers' =&gt; [
    'accept' =&gt; 'text/plain'
  ],
]);
$data = $response-&gt;getBody()-&gt;getContents();
dpm($data);
</code></pre><p>4. visit "/admin/reports/http-client-log"</p>";s:7:"summary";s:196:"Log all drupal core http_client request &amp; response logs in database. So it easily to track the outgoing traffic init by drupal http_client.
