a:54:{s:4:"body";a:3:{s:5:"value";s:1116:"<p>Allows bundle classes to be configured using annotations. This removes the need to implement <code class="language-php">hook_entity_bundle_info_alter()</code>.</p>
<h2>Example</h2>
<pre class="codeblock"><code class="language-php">&lt;?php

namespace Drupal\my_module\Entity\Node;

use Drupal\Core\Annotation\Translation;
use Drupal\node\Entity\Node;

/**
 * @Bundle(
 *   entity_type = "node",
 *   bundle = "article",
 *   label = @Translation("Article"),
 * )
 */
class Article extends Node { }
</code></pre><h2>Attributes</h2>
<p>In the future it may be possible to use attributes instead of annotations. See <span class="project-issue-issue-link project-issue-status-info project-issue-status-8"><a href="/project/drupal/issues/3252386" title="Status: Needs review">#3252386: Use PHP attributes instead of doctrine annotations</a></span> for the core issue where this is being developed. The 2.x branch of this module supports using attributes with a core patch from this issue. See the <a href="https://git.drupalcode.org/project/bca/-/blob/2.x/README.md" rel="nofollow">2.x README</a> for more details.</p>";s:7:"summary";s:198:"Allows bundle classes to be configured using annotations. This removes the need to implement hook_entity_bundle_info_alter().
Example
