a:54:{s:22:"taxonomy_vocabulary_44";a:1:{s:2:"id";s:5:"13028";}s:22:"taxonomy_vocabulary_46";a:1:{s:2:"id";s:4:"9988";}s:21:"taxonomy_vocabulary_3";a:1:{i:0;a:1:{s:2:"id";s:2:"59";}}s:6:"upload";a:3:{i:0;a:3:{s:4:"file";a:3:{s:3:"uri";s:42:"https://www.drupal.org/api-d7/file/6647900";s:2:"id";s:7:"6647900";s:8:"resource";s:4:"file";}s:11:"description";s:22:"Map values with Fluent";s:7:"display";s:1:"1";}i:1;a:3:{s:4:"file";a:3:{s:3:"uri";s:42:"https://www.drupal.org/api-d7/file/6647917";s:2:"id";s:7:"6647917";s:8:"resource";s:4:"file";}s:11:"description";s:0:"";s:7:"display";s:1:"1";}i:2;a:3:{s:4:"file";a:3:{s:3:"uri";s:42:"https://www.drupal.org/api-d7/file/6647924";s:2:"id";s:7:"6647924";s:8:"resource";s:4:"file";}s:11:"description";s:0:"";s:7:"display";s:1:"1";}}s:4:"body";a:3:{s:5:"value";s:2998:"<p><strong>Documentation WIP:</strong></p>
<p>Fluent improves the development experience simplifying the code to access a fieldable entity (Node, Media, Taxonomy Term, Paragraphs...).</p>
<p>For multi-value fields Fluent integrates <a href="https://laravel.com/docs/9.x/collections" title="Laravel Collections" rel="nofollow">Laravel Collections</a> to post-process the returned values.</p>
<h2>What module does?</h2>
<p>Fluent contains the below methods for Fieldables Entities:<br />
<img src="/files/project-images/Usage.png" alt="Fluent functions" /></p>
<h2>Welcome to the dot notation</h2>
<p>The dot notation is a hierarchical sequence of field names linked to each other that will take along to the resolution of the field value.</p>
<p><code class="language-php">field_media.uid.email</code></p>
<h2>Multi Value Fields</h2>
<p>When you access to a multi value field usually your next task is convert value by value in something else, Fluent integrates Laravel Collections improving your syntax using methods that operate over the data in your field.</p>
<p>For example:<br />
<img src="/files/map values.png" alt="map values with Fluent" /></p>
<h3>Get multiple fields in one call.</h3>
<pre class="codeblock"><code class="language-php">using($node)-&gt;values([
  'time' =&gt; 'field_date_time',
  'media_names'=&gt; 'field_media.label',
  'term_urls'=&gt; 'field_tags.url',
  'id' =&gt; 'nid',
  'title',
])-&gt;all();

// Result
^ array:5 [▼
  "time" =&gt; Drupal\Core\Datetime\DrupalDateTime {#1373 ▶}
  "media_names" =&gt; array:3 [▼
    0 =&gt; "Image 1"
    1 =&gt; "Image 2"
    2 =&gt; "Image 3"
  ]
  "term_urls" =&gt; array:3 [▼
    0 =&gt; Drupal\Core\Url {#1540 ▶}
    1 =&gt; Drupal\Core\Url {#1547 ▶}
    2 =&gt; Drupal\Core\Url {#1548 ▶}
  ]
  "id" =&gt; 1
  "title" =&gt; "title Boolean"
]
</code></pre><p>
The goal is support multiple behaviors dependent of the field if the field don't have a custom behavior by default return the raw value.</p>
<pre class="codeblock"><code class="language-php">// Latest revision of the node
$latestRevision = using($node)-&gt;value('vid');
// Result:
Drupal\node\Entity\Node {#1966 ▶}

// All revisions of the node
$allRevisions = using($node)-&gt;values('vid');
// Result:
Drupal\fluent\Collection {#1689 ▼
  #items: array:3 [▼
    0 =&gt; Drupal\node\Entity\Node {#1811 ▶}
    1 =&gt; Drupal\node\Entity\Node {#1820 ▶}
    2 =&gt; Drupal\node\Entity\Node {#1967 ▶}
  ]
}
</code></pre><h2>Useful errors</h2>
<p>Made a typo writing the name of your field?<br />
<img src="/files/Field%20not%20found.png" height="150" alt="List of fields if field doen't exist" /></p>
