a:54:{s:4:"body";a:3:{s:5:"value";s:508:"<p>This module provides a simple Filter plugin type that wraps processed text output in an html element with customizable classing.</p>
<p>Typically, this is how I've solved what I've dubbed the "last child" problem with unpredictable content.  By identifying such content via a CSS class, one can take the following approach to normalizing front-end display:</p>
<pre class="codeblock"><code class="language-php">.wysiwyg {
  display: contents;
}

.wysiwyg *:last-child {
  margin-bottom: 0;
}
</code></pre>";s:7:"summary";s:200:"This module provides a simple Filter plugin type that wraps processed text output in an html element with customizable classing.
